Download methodology brief (PDF, 24pp)
</a> </div> <div class="prose" data-astro-cid-kf663cba> <h3 style="margin-top: 0;" data-astro-cid-kf663cba>How we measure</h3> <p data-astro-cid-kf663cba>Every program in our portfolio is bound by the same five-pillar rhythm: diagnose, design, deliver, document, distribute. The measurement work happens at the diagnose and document ends — and we use the same instruments year-on-year so that the numbers are comparable across cycles.</p> <p data-astro-cid-kf663cba>For LCASP and Summer School, we administer a baseline assessment within the first week of intake and an endline within the last week of the same term. Both use a partner-verified instrument adapted from the EGRA (Early Grade Reading Assessment) framework. For NextGen Genius Club, the unit of measurement is project completion and public-exhibition presentation — we record both per-child. For STREET Storm, we follow each participant for six months post-program and record their employment, apprenticeship or further-study status.</p> <p data-astro-cid-kf663cba>Where we have revised a previously-published number, the case-study table flags it. Where a pilot did not yield a statistically significant gain, we publish the finding and retire the pilot.</p> <h3 data-astro-cid-kf663cba>What we don't claim</h3> <p data-astro-cid-kf663cba>We do not control for prior schooling outside our partner schools. We do not claim that improvements in our programs are causally attributable to our work — only that the children in our cohorts moved between baseline and endline. Where appropriate we discuss confounding factors in the case-study notes.</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section class="section" style="padding-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 96px; background: var(--surface); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);" data-screen-label="Impact · Case studies" data-astro-cid-kf663cba> <div class="section-inner" data-astro-cid-kf663cba> <div class="what-head" data-astro-cid-kf663cba> <div 